    "## 2. Selecting the XRB population\n",
    "\n",
    "Out of the entire population that we simulated, only a small fraction are potentially XRBs. So we do not need to be carrying everything around. To do that, we are gonna try to follow as closely as possible the tutorial on [\"Transient populations\"](https://posydon.org/POSYDON/latest/tutorials-examples/population-synthesis/bbh_analysis.html). You can consult that for inspiration. However, since here we are dealing with XRBs and not transients, some of the steps will have to be adapted.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5482c6e8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div class='alert alert-success'>\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exercise 2: Select candidate XRBs\n",
    "\n",
    "Filter the population to select potential XRBs. One component must be a\n",
    "neutron star or black hole, while the other must be a normal, non-compact star.\n",
    "Remove systems disrupted during a supernova, failed systems, and initially\n",
    "overflowing systems. Save the indices into a list named `selected_indices`.\n",
    "\n",
    "</div>\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6af97119",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div class=\"alert alert-warning\" style=\"margin-top: 20px\">\n",
    "<details>\n",
    "\n",
    "<b><summary>Hint (click to reveal):</summary></b>\n",
    "\n",
    "Besides `NS` and `BH`, exclude `WD` and `massless_remnant` from the possible\n",
    "donor states. Create a temporary table from `oneline` containing\n",
    "`S1_state_f`, `S2_state_f`, and `state_f`, then build a Boolean mask.\n",
    "\n",
    "The condition should allow either S1 to be the compact object and S2 the\n",
    "donor, or S2 to be the compact object and S1 the donor. It should not select a\n",
    "double compact object.\n",
    "\n",
    "</details>\n",
    "</div>\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3e9f88c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Write your code for Exercise 2 here.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f0c01f46",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div class=\"alert alert-warning\" style=\"margin-top: 20px\">\n",
    "<details>\n",
    "\n",
    "<b><summary>Solution (click to reveal):</summary></b>\n",
    "\n",
    "~~~python\n",
    "tmp_data = pop.oneline.select(\n",
    "    columns=[\"state_f\", \"S1_state_f\", \"S2_state_f\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "S1_state = tmp_data[\"S1_state_f\"]\n",
    "S2_state = tmp_data[\"S2_state_f\"]\n",
    "binary_state = tmp_data[\"state_f\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# A potential XRB must contain one compact object and one\n",
    "# non-compact donor star.\n",
    "compact_objects = {\"BH\", \"NS\"}\n",
    "not_donor_stars = {\"BH\", \"NS\", \"WD\", \"massless_remnant\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "has_compact_object_and_donor = (\n",
    "    S1_state.isin(compact_objects)\n",
    "    & ~S2_state.isin(not_donor_stars)\n",
    ") | (\n",
    "    S2_state.isin(compact_objects)\n",
    "    & ~S1_state.isin(not_donor_stars)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Exclude systems that are no longer bound or did not evolve successfully.\n",
    "invalid_binary_states = {\"disrupted\", \"ERR\", \"initial_RLOF\"}\n",
    "is_valid_binary = ~binary_state.isin(invalid_binary_states)\n",
    "\n",
    "mask = has_compact_object_and_donor & is_valid_binary\n",
    "selected_indices = tmp_data.index[mask].to_list()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Selected {len(selected_indices):,} potential XRBs\")\n",
    "pop.oneline[selected_indices]\n",
    "~~~\n",
    "\n",
    "</details>\n",
    "</div>\n"
   ]
  },
