    "### 2.2 RLO, wind-fed, and Be-XRB channels\n",
    "\n",
    "We separate three different types of XRBs based on the accretion mechanism:\n",
    "- **Roche-lobe overflow (RLO):** the donor fills its Roche lobe and matter\n",
    "  flows through the inner Lagrange point. We use POSYDON's mass-transfer rate\n",
    "  as the supplied accretion rate.\n",
    "- **Wind-fed XRB:** a detached compact object captures a fraction of the\n",
    "  donor's wind. `wind_velocity` estimates the terminal speed, and\n",
    "  `bondi_hoyle_accretion_rate` evaluates the deterministic orbit-averaged\n",
    "  Bondi–Hoyle–Lyttleton capture rate.\n",
    "- **Be-XRB:** a rapidly rotating H-rich B star can supply a decretion disc.\n",
    "  The notebook identifies plausible systems, while `be_xray_luminosity`\n",
    "  provides the empirical orbital-period–luminosity relation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The wind velocity prescription uses the donor's helium-core mass as an evolutionary\n",
    "proxy.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this tutorial, a detached candidate is labeled Be when the donor is an\n",
    "H-rich core-H-burning star with $M\\geq6\\,M_\\odot$, surface rotation at least\n",
    "70% of critical, $10\\leq P_{\\mathrm{orb}}\\leq300$ days, and a notional\n",
    "decretion disc extending to 100 stellar radii that reaches the donor's\n",
    "periastron Roche lobe. We assign a 30% duty cycle later. This is a model choice\n",
    "and a source of major uncertainty.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the `XRB_selection_function`, we implement the code for these selections.\n",
    "This is a long function as we includes both the selection and calculation of the X-ray luminosities for each system."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8396699f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def XRB_selection_function(history_chunk, oneline_chunk,\n",
    "                           formation_channels_chunk=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Create the snapshot XRB table and calculate X-ray luminosities.\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    indices = oneline_chunk.index.to_numpy()\n",
    "    df_XRBs = pd.DataFrame(index=indices)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # General binary properties\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"time\"] = oneline_chunk[\"time_f\"] * 1.0e-6  # Myr\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"time_of_birth\"] = oneline_chunk[\"time_i\"] * 1.0e-6  # Myr\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"metallicity\"] = oneline_chunk[\"metallicity\"]\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"binary_state\"] = oneline_chunk[\"state_f\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    compact_types = {\"BH\", \"NS\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "    s1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_state_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    s2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_state_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    is1 = np.isin(s1, list(compact_types))\n",
    "    is2 = np.isin(s2, list(compact_types))\n",
    "    one_compact = is1 ^ is2           # exactly one compact star\n",
    "    accretor_is_1 = one_compact & is1 # compact star is S1\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def pick(v1, v2, fill=np.nan):\n",
    "        \"\"\"v1 where the compact star is S1, v2 where it is S2, else fill.\"\"\"\n",
    "        return np.where(one_compact, np.where(accretor_is_1, v1, v2), fill)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "    m1  = oneline_chunk[\"S1_mass_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    m2  = oneline_chunk[\"S2_mass_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    log_r1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_log_R_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    log_r2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_log_R_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    log_l1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_log_L_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    log_l2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_log_L_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    lg_m1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_lg_mdot_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    lg_m2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_lg_mdot_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    sh1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_surface_h1_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    sh2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_surface_h1_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    hc1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_he_core_mass_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    hc2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_he_core_mass_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    rot1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_surf_avg_omega_div_omega_crit_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    rot2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_surf_avg_omega_div_omega_crit_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    sp1 = oneline_chunk[\"S1_spin_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    sp2 = oneline_chunk[\"S2_spin_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_mass\"] = pick(m2, m1)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"accretor_mass\"] = pick(m1, m2)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_state\"] = pick(s2, s1, fill=None)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"accretor_state\"] = pick(s1, s2, fill=None)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_radius\"] = pick(10.0**log_r2, 10.0**log_r1)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"accretor_radius\"] = pick(10.0**log_r1, 10.0**log_r2)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_luminosity\"] = pick(10.0**log_l2, 10.0**log_l1)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_mass_loss_rate\"] = pick(10.0**lg_m2, 10.0**lg_m1)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_surface_h1\"] = pick(sh2, sh1)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_he_core_mass\"] = pick(hc2, hc1)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_rotation_fraction\"] = pick(rot2, rot1)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"accretor_spin\"] = pick(sp1, sp2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Binary-level properties\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"orbital_period\"] = oneline_chunk[\"orbital_period_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"eccentricity\"] = oneline_chunk[\"eccentricity_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"rlo_mass_transfer_rate\"] = (\n",
    "        10.0**oneline_chunk[\"lg_mtransfer_rate_f\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Stars without a defined helium core are assigned zero core mass.\n",
    "    valid_he_core = (\n",
    "        np.isfinite(df_XRBs[\"donor_he_core_mass\"])\n",
    "        & (df_XRBs[\"donor_he_core_mass\"] >= 0.0)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_he_core_mass\"] = np.where(\n",
    "        valid_he_core, df_XRBs[\"donor_he_core_mass\"], 0.0\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    # Classify the accretion mode\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"orbital_separation\"] = orbital_separation_from_period(\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"orbital_period\"].to_numpy(float),\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"accretor_mass\"].to_numpy(float),\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_mass\"].to_numpy(float),\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    periastron_separation = (\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"orbital_separation\"].to_numpy(float)\n",
    "        * (1.0 - df_XRBs[\"eccentricity\"].to_numpy(float))\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"donor_roche_lobe_periastron\"] = roche_lobe_radius(\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_mass\"].to_numpy(float),\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"accretor_mass\"].to_numpy(float),\n",
    "        periastron_separation,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    detached = df_XRBs[\"binary_state\"] == \"detached\"\n",
    "    rlo = df_XRBs[\"binary_state\"].isin([\"RLO1\", \"RLO2\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Approximate selection of Be-XRBs.\n",
    "    be = (\n",
    "        detached\n",
    "        & (df_XRBs[\"donor_state\"] == \"H-rich_Core_H_burning\")\n",
    "        & (df_XRBs[\"donor_mass\"] >= 6.0)\n",
    "        & (df_XRBs[\"donor_rotation_fraction\"] >= 0.7)\n",
    "        & df_XRBs[\"orbital_period\"].between(10.0, 300.0)\n",
    "        & (\n",
    "            df_XRBs[\"donor_roche_lobe_periastron\"]\n",
    "            <= 100.0 * df_XRBs[\"donor_radius\"]\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    wind = detached & ~be\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"accretion_mode\"] = np.select(\n",
    "        [be, rlo, wind],\n",
    "        [\"Be\", \"RLO\", \"wind\"],\n",
    "        default=\"other\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    # Calculate the radiative efficiency\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "    is_bh = df_XRBs[\"accretor_state\"] == \"BH\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    # If the BH spin is unavailable, assume a non-spinning BH.\n",
    "    bh_spin = df_XRBs[\"accretor_spin\"].to_numpy(float)\n",
    "    bh_spin = np.where(np.isfinite(bh_spin), bh_spin, 0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # If the NS radius is unavailable, assume a radius of 12.5 km.\n",
    "    ns_radius = df_XRBs[\"accretor_radius\"].to_numpy(float)\n",
    "    ns_radius = np.where(\n",
    "        np.isfinite(ns_radius) & (ns_radius > 0.0),\n",
    "        ns_radius,\n",
    "        1.25e6 / const.Rsun,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    bh_efficiency = black_hole_radiative_efficiency(bh_spin)\n",
    "    ns_efficiency = neutron_star_radiative_efficiency(\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"accretor_mass\"], ns_radius\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"radiative_efficiency\"] = np.where(\n",
    "        is_bh, bh_efficiency, ns_efficiency\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    # Calculate the wind-accretion rate\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "    # For detached systems, the donor mass-loss rate is interpreted\n",
    "    # as the stellar wind mass-loss rate.\n",
    "    donor_wind_velocity = wind_velocity(\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_mass\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_radius\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_luminosity\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_mass_loss_rate\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_surface_h1\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_he_core_mass\"],\n",
    "        scheme=\"Kudritzki+2000\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"wind_velocity\"] = donor_wind_velocity\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"wind_accretion_rate\"] = bondi_hoyle_accretion_rate(\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"accretor_mass\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_mass\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_mass_loss_rate\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"orbital_separation\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"eccentricity\"],\n",
    "        donor_wind_velocity,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # RLO systems use the mass-transfer rate; detached systems use BHL.\n",
    "    supplied_accretion_rate = np.where(\n",
    "        rlo,\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"rlo_mass_transfer_rate\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"wind_accretion_rate\"],\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "    # Calculate the X-ray luminosities\n",
    "    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "    luminosity, beaming_factor, Eddington_ratio = accretion_luminosity(\n",
    "        supplied_accretion_rate,\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"accretor_mass\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"donor_surface_h1\"],\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"radiative_efficiency\"],\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Convert bolometric luminosity to the adopted X-ray band.\n",
    "    classical_xray_luminosity = 0.5 * luminosity\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"L_bol_iso\"] = luminosity\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"beaming_factor\"] = beaming_factor\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"Eddington_ratio\"] = Eddington_ratio\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"Lx_rlo\"] = np.where(rlo, classical_xray_luminosity, 0.0)\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"Lx_bhl\"] = np.where(wind, classical_xray_luminosity, 0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Be-XRB luminosities use the empirical period–luminosity relation.\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"Lx_be\"] = 0.0\n",
    "    df_XRBs.loc[be, \"Lx_be\"] = be_xray_luminosity(\n",
    "        df_XRBs.loc[be, \"orbital_period\"]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Be-XRB luminosities are treated as isotropic.\n",
    "    df_XRBs.loc[be, \"beaming_factor\"] = 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"Lx_tot\"] = df_XRBs[\n",
    "        [\"Lx_rlo\", \"Lx_bhl\", \"Lx_be\"]\n",
    "    ].sum(axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Adopt a 30% duty cycle for Be-XRB outbursts.\n",
    "    df_XRBs[\"duty_cycle\"] = np.where(be, 0.3, 1.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if formation_channels_chunk is not None:\n",
    "        df_XRBs[\"formation_channel\"] = formation_channels_chunk.loc[\n",
    "            df_XRBs.index, \"channel\"\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Return only RLO, wind-fed, and Be X-ray binaries.\n",
    "    return df_XRBs.loc[df_XRBs[\"accretion_mode\"] != \"other\"]"
   ]
  },
